# Tailwind canonical classes

When writing or editing Tailwind classes, prefer **canonical utilities** from the project's design system over arbitrary values and legacy v3 aliases.

## Prefer

- Theme tokens defined in `app/globals.css` (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `font-sans`, etc.)
- Standard scale utilities (`mt-4`, `rounded-lg`, `text-zinc-600`) over arbitrary values (`mt-[16px]`, `rounded-[8px]`)
- v4 canonical names: `shrink-0` not `flex-shrink-0`, `grow` not `flex-grow`, `bg-linear-to-*` not `bg-gradient-to-*`

## Avoid (unless no theme equivalent exists)

- Arbitrary values: `w-[158px]`, `bg-[#383838]`, `text-[red]`
- Arbitrary opacity: `border-black/[.08]` — use `border-black/10` or a theme color
- Legacy v3 aliases that have v4 replacements

## When arbitrary values are OK

- One-off values with no close scale match **and** no theme token
- Complex selectors that have no canonical variant (rare)

## Examples from this project

```tsx
// ❌
className="hover:bg-[#383838] md:w-[158px] border-black/[.08]"

// ✅
className="hover:bg-zinc-800 md:w-40 border-black/10"
// or, for brand colors:
className="bg-foreground text-background hover:bg-foreground/90"
```

When touching existing non-canonical classes, convert them to canonical equivalents where the design system provides a match.
